ief. In the first sense, we aim to believe what is most probably true according to our total evidence, including testimony from peers and authorities. In the second, we aim to base our beliefs only on objective evidence and argumentation, even if that lowers the probability of their being true. The first principle of rational belief tends to serve the short-term epistemic interests of individuals, while the second tends to serve the long-term epistemic interests of both individuals and groups. The best way to reconcile these principles in cases of peer disagreement is to associate them with two corresponding species of belief, here called perception and opinion."}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/W2336005475", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199226078.003.0007", "title": "Peer Disagreement and Higher‐Order Evidence", "publication_year": 2010, "type": "book-chapter", "cited_by_count": 580, "open_access": {"is_oa": true, "oa_status": "green", "oa_url": "https://philpapers.org/archive/KELPDA.pdf", "any_repository_has_fulltext": true}, "primary_location": {"id": "doi:10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199226078.003.0007", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199226078.003.0007", "is_oa": false, "landing_page_url": "https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199226078.003.0007", "pdf_url": null, "source": {"id": "https://openalex.org/S4306463708", "display_name": "Oxford University Press eBooks", "issn_l": null, "issn": null, "is_oa": false, "is_in_doaj": false, "is_core": false, "listed_in": [], "host_organization": "https://openalex.org/P4310311648", "host_organization_name": "Oxford University Press", "host_organization_lineage": ["https://openalex.org/P4310311648", "https://openalex.org/P4310311647"], "host_organization_lineage_names": ["Oxford University Press", "University of Oxford"], "type": "ebook platform"}, "license": null, "license_id": null, "version": "publishedVersion", "is_accepted": true, "is_published": true, "raw_source_name": "Disagreement", "ra